From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: build <build@localhost>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:54:19 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt6797: restart the WLAN when a closed interface is
 brought up

Taking an interface down closes this driver instance for good, and bringing an
interface up again was refused with -EOPNOTSUPP until the module was reloaded.
networkd brought a fresh wlan0 up and down before iwd replaced it with its own,
and the new interface could never start. Ask CONSYS for a WLAN restart there, as
a scan on a closed instance already does: a new phy comes back, and iwd and
networkd take it up.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c
index 6eb62daab..10f14bab4 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c
@@ -1169,6 +1169,12 @@ static int mt6797_mac_start(struct ieee80211_hw *hw)
 	    !mac->first_error && !mac->join_closed) {
 		mac->started = true;
 		ret = 0;
+	} else if (mac->closing || mac->first_error || mac->join_closed) {
+		/* Taking an interface down closes this instance for good, and iwd
+		 * and networkd do that in turn. A restart brings back a new phy,
+		 * which they take up again.
+		 */
+		mt6797_consys_wlan_request_restart();
 	}
 	mutex_unlock(&mac->mutex);
 	return ret;
-- 
